- severity: Low
  category: dry.missing-abstraction
  file: src/Base/Parameter.cpp
  line: 1886
  title: Entity-resolution hardening is written out by hand in LoadDocument, and the sibling parser in CheckDocument (same file) didn't get the new resolver
  evidence: |
    // LoadDocument (new code, 1880-1887)
    auto entityBlocker = std::make_unique<NoOpEntityResolver>();
    ...
    parser->setDisableDefaultEntityResolution(true);
    parser->setEntityResolver(entityBlocker.get());

    // CheckDocument (existing, 2091-2108)
    XercesDOMParser parser;
    ...
    parser.setDisableDefaultEntityResolution(true);

    DOMTreeErrorReporter errHandler;
    parser.setErrorHandler(&errHandler);
    parser.parse(xmlFile);
  impact: Parameter.cpp has two XercesDOMParser setups that parse the same user-parameter XML. Both already repeat the "disable default entity resolution + attach DOMTreeErrorReporter" setup. This change adds a second hardening step (`setEntityResolver`) to only one of them. The two setups now differ, and CheckDocument still parses the same file with Xerces' default entity handling. The next fix to parser hardening would also have to be made in two places.
  remedy: Put the hardening in one file-local helper next to `NoOpEntityResolver`, for example `static void hardenParser(XercesDOMParser& p, EntityResolver& r) { p.setDisableDefaultEntityResolution(true); p.setEntityResolver(&r); }`, or keep one static `NoOpEntityResolver` instance. Call it from LoadDocument (src/Base/Parameter.cpp:1886-1887) and CheckDocument (src/Base/Parameter.cpp:2105), then delete the separate `setDisableDefaultEntityResolution` calls. Don't add a third copy. Nothing else in the repo defines an `EntityResolver` (searched src/, not counting 3rdParty), so this class is not a reinvented utility. It is the only place to put the shared setup.
  evidence_refs: [src/Base/Parameter.cpp:2091, src/Base/Parameter.cpp:2105, src/Base/Parameter.cpp:2107]
  confidence: medium
  overlap_hints: [security.xxe, correctness.partial-fix, craft.abstraction]

What else I checked, none of it worth a separate finding:
- **No existing resolver to reuse:** a repo-wide search for `EntityResolver` / `resolveEntity` found nothing outside this change. `NoOpEntityResolver` duplicates nothing.
- **Other Xerces parsers use a different shared setup:** src/App/ProjectFile.cpp:242-247, src/Mod/Mesh/App/Core/IO/Reader3MF.cpp:115-124 (`makeDomParser`), src/App/Metadata.cpp:144-148 and src/Base/Reader.cpp:78 share a similar setup of their own. None of them has `setDisableDefaultEntityResolution` or a resolver, so this change doesn't copy from them. Whether they need the same hardening is a security question, not a DRY one.
- **PreCompiled.h:** the duplicated `SAXParseException.hpp` include (lines 106 and 109) and duplicated `sax2/Attributes.hpp` include (lines 111 and 113) were already there. The new line 107 just sits between them and adds no new duplicate.

